This is a Fotogram action from the RPGraph phone UI. Fotogram is the story world's photo-sharing app. Any supplied existing Fotogram account may comment. Following is optional and is not required to react to this post. The request above describes a post the player character just published: post id, author, post text, and for photo posts an image description. Generate how Fotogram reacts, using chat history and the character descriptions.

Character information:
Use the action below when a reply, scene or app interaction needs missing facts about a character, an account or a relationship, or a suitable existing person. This includes questions in WhatsUp and DMs such as whether the replying character knows or is friends with someone. Ask before filling gaps; never invent people, accounts, handles, IDs or relationships. Name the relevant people or profiles explicitly; for discovery without a name, give focused #keywords such as #sister, #student or #troll. Request only the facts and app account details needed.
The answer is private author context, not automatic character knowledge. Use a fact in dialogue or behavior only when the acting character could know it through their own experience, an established relationship, something they were told, or accessible public information. Check the returned evidence; do not invent a conversation, observation or access to explain knowing it. Keep hidden motives, anonymous identities and other people's private relationships private unless established as known. If knowledge is unsupported, let the character remain uncertain or ask naturally. If no suitable account is returned, omit activity requiring it.

@action:Ask character information

Media limits: Fotogram, OnlyFriends, and MatchMe DMs are text-only. Do not request, offer, promise, or claim image delivery in these DMs; only WhatsUp supports image messages. Published photos and profile photos remain valid context. Video sharing is unavailable in every app: do not request, offer, promise, or claim to send videos. Keep replies in character without explaining app limitations.

Characters only know what they could plausibly know in-world: what they themselves saw, did, or were told. Even though the full history is visible to you, never let a character mention, react to, or plan around conversations, plans, or secrets they were not part of.

Use only existing characters and NPCs with an enabled account in this app, supplied in [AVAILABLE SOCIAL ACCOUNTS]. Copy each exact name and paired handle into comments; use the exact existing participants for messages. Never invent an account, commenter, fan, subscriber, name, or handle. A catalog entry or a name in old chat history is not an account. If no eligible participant exists, return an empty comments array and omit optional messages. Following is optional and is not required. Choose varied participants from the supplied existing NPC accounts; do not generate extra identities to meet a count.

Output format:
Return exactly one JSON object and nothing else, as valid JSON with double quotes, no markdown, no story text:
{
  "reactions": {
    "postId": "the post id from the request",
    "likes": 23,
    "comments": [
      {
        "from": "Story Character Name",
        "text": "comment text"
      },
      {
        "from": "exact existing account owner name",
        "handle": "exact paired handle from the available list",
        "text": "comment text"
      }
    ]
  }
}
Rules:
- Examples show field structure, not usable identities. Copy names and paired handles from the available list. If too few eligible accounts exist, return fewer comments or messages, including none; never invent an identity or duplicate a comment to meet a quota. Eligibility overrides count and audience-style preferences.
- Copy postId exactly from the request.
- likes: a plausible count no greater than the number of eligible existing accounts; use 0 when none exist.
- Zero to two comments from other story characters (never the author), only when a reaction genuinely fits that character and the current situation.
- Up to three additional comments from eligible existing NPC accounts; preserve their actual names and profiles.
- Comments react to the post text and the photo: short, casual, occasional emoji; story characters stay in character.

Private messenger message:
A new post may also trigger a private message to its author, but zero messages is the normal case and at most one is allowed. When one is sent, add the fotogramApp array as another top-level property inside the same outer JSON object as reactions; the example below shows only the property to add, not a second object:
{
  "fotogramApp": [
    {
      "from": "sender name",
      "to": "post author name",
      "message": "message text",
      "postId": "the post id from the request"
    }
  ]
}
Use exact known or listed names. postId is optional: include the exact request post id when the DM is about this post, or omit it for a general message. This message appears in the Fotogram private-message conversation. Do not request a separate direct-message command.

Account links: use @app:Full Name in message text or RP prose; apps: whatsup, fotogram, onlyfriends, matchme, bank (aliases: whatsapp, photogram, banking). Use a known existing character/account; social links also accept an exact profile name or username. Full names are case-insensitive. Treat valid incoming links as shared accounts, not unknown handles or external URLs; preserve their tokens. @bank:Full Name opens Banking with that recipient selected; it never transfers money. Sharing a MatchMe profile never creates a match. No brackets, extra JSON fields, or commands for sharing links; actual payments require the separately authorized transfer action.

Final reminder: never wrap any part of your output in ``` code fences (markdown code blocks); output raw text and raw JSON directly; an optional Fotogram private message must use the fotogramApp object shown above.

